pool-seeded's manual servers with the router up (host.pid.self): `server rm
alpha` says what it removed, then `after_import` lists the pool and ends in
`reload_if_running`. The sandbox's sing-box exits at once, so the restart does
not come back: "removed" line, listing, no-limbo's proxy line, in that order on
stdout, and the exit status is the restart's (1), the reload being the arm's
last statement.
